---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Thesis from '../components/Thesis.astro';
---

<Layout title="MLS — Everything is MLS">
  <!-- 1. Intro -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container-x max-w-3xl">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-6 reveal">The idea</p>
      <h1 class="headline text-6xl md:text-8xl text-white leading-none mb-10 reveal">
        Multi-Level<br /><span class="text-cyan-glow">Selection</span>
      </h1>

      <div class="space-y-6 text-white/75 text-lg leading-relaxed reveal">
        <p>
          Multi-Level Selection is a way of understanding evolution that doesn’t
          stop at the individual. The familiar story says natural selection works
          on single organisms, each competing to survive and reproduce. MLS says
          that’s only part of the picture: selection also acts on groups.
        </p>
        <p>
          A group of cooperators can out-compete a group of cheaters — even when,
          inside each group, the cheaters are doing better than the cooperators
          next to them. That tension between what’s good for the individual and
          what’s good for the group turns out to run through almost everything:
          how cells became bodies, how bodies became societies, and how a
          neighborhood, a company, or a city either holds together or comes apart.
        </p>
        <p>
          On this show we use MLS as a lens. Once you can see the levels —
          individual and group, pulling in different directions at the same time —
          a lot of modern life starts to make a different kind of sense.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2. The New Paradigm (callout) -->
  <section class="section section-tight">
    <div class="container-x max-w-3xl">
      <div class="edge-card p-10 md:p-14 reveal" style="border-color:rgba(0,212,212,0.3)">
        <p class="eyebrow mb-6">The New Paradigm</p>
        <p class="headline text-3xl md:text-4xl text-white leading-tight mb-4">
          A fuller account is on its way.
        </p>
        <p class="text-white/55 text-lg leading-relaxed">
          Write-up coming soon from David Sloan Wilson.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3. The thesis, stated cold -->
  <Thesis />
</Layout>
